  93:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
  94:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** * Description: This function is used to obtain the name assigned to a semaphore, mutex, mailbox or 
  95:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
  96:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** * Arguments  : pevent    is a pointer to the event group.  'pevent' can point either to a semaphore
  97:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                        a mutex, a mailbox or a queue.  Where this function is concerned, the actu
  98:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                        type is irrelevant.
  99:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
 100:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              pname     is a pointer to a pointer to an ASCII string that will receive the name of
 101:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                        mutex, mailbox or queue.
 102:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
 103:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              perr      is a pointer to an error code that can contain one of the following values
 104:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
 105:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                        OS_ERR_NONE                if the name was copied to 'pname'
 106:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                        OS_ERR_EVENT_TYPE          if 'pevent' is not pointing to the proper event
 107:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                                                   control block type.
 108:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                        OS_ERR_PNAME_NULL          You passed a NULL pointer for 'pname'
 109:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                        OS_ERR_PEVENT_NULL         if you passed a NULL pointer for 'pevent'
 110:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                        OS_ERR_NAME_GET_ISR        if you are trying to call this function from an
 111:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
 112:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** * Returns    : The length of the string or 0 if the 'pevent' is a NULL pointer.
 113:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 114:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** */
