 248:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** /*
 249:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 250:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                                       PEND ON MULTIPLE EVENTS
 251:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
 252:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** * Description: This function waits for multiple events.  If multiple events are ready at the start 
 253:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              pend call, then all available events are returned as ready.  If the task must pend o
 254:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              multiple events, then only the first posted or aborted event is returned as ready.
 255:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
 256:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** * Arguments  : pevents_pend  is a pointer to a NULL-terminated array of event control blocks to wai
 257:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
 258:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              pevents_rdy   is a pointer to an array to return which event control blocks are avai
 259:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            or ready.  The size of the array MUST be greater than or equal to the 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccMSGEvU.s 			page 6


 260:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            of the 'pevents_pend' array, including terminating NULL.
 261:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
 262:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              pmsgs_rdy     is a pointer to an array to return messages from any available message
 263:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            events.  The size of the array MUST be greater than or equal to the si
 264:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            the 'pevents_pend' array, excluding the terminating NULL.  Since NULL
 265:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            messages are valid messages, this array cannot be NULL-terminated.  In
 266:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            every available message-type event returns its messages in the 'pmsgs_
 267:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            array at the same index as the event is returned in the 'pevents_rdy' 
 268:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            All other 'pmsgs_rdy' array indices are filled with NULL messages.
 269:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
 270:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              timeout       is an optional timeout period (in clock ticks).  If non-zero, your tas
 271:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            wait for the resources up to the amount of time specified by this argu
 272:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            If you specify 0, however, your task will wait forever for the specifi
 273:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            events or, until the resources becomes available (or the events occur)
 274:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
