 649:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
 650:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** * Notes      : 1) This function should be called with interrupts already disabled
 651:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              2) Your ISR can directly increment OSIntNesting without calling this function becaus
 652:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                 OSIntNesting has been declared 'global'.
 653:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              3) You MUST still call OSIntExit() even though you increment OSIntNesting directly.
 654:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              4) You MUST invoke OSIntEnter() and OSIntExit() in pair.  In other words, for every 
 655:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                 to OSIntEnter() at the beginning of the ISR you MUST have a call to OSIntExit() a
 656:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                 end of the ISR.
 657:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              5) You are allowed to nest interrupts up to 255 levels deep.
 658:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              6) I removed the OS_ENTER_CRITICAL() and OS_EXIT_CRITICAL() around the increment bec
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccMSGEvU.s 			page 13


 659:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                 OSIntEnter() is always called with interrupts disabled.
 660:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 661:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** */
 662:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** 
 663:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** void  OSIntEnter (void)
 664:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** {
 665:./ucos/Core/os_core.c ****     if (OSRunning == OS_TRUE) {
 666:./ucos/Core/os_core.c ****         if (OSIntNesting < 255u) {
