1981:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** /*
1982:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
1983:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                                           INITIALIZE TCB
1984:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
1985:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** * Description: This function is internal to uC/OS-II and is used to initialize a Task Control Block
1986:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              a task is created (see OSTaskCreate() and OSTaskCreateExt()).
1987:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
1988:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** * Arguments  : prio          is the priority of the task being created
1989:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
1990:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              ptos          is a pointer to the task's top-of-stack assuming that the CPU register
1991:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            have been placed on the stack.  Note that the top-of-stack corresponds
1992:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            'high' memory location is OS_STK_GROWTH is set to 1 and a 'low' memory
1993:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            location if OS_STK_GROWTH is set to 0.  Note that stack growth is CPU
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccMSGEvU.s 			page 113


1994:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            specific.
1995:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
1996:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              pbos          is a pointer to the bottom of stack.  A NULL pointer is passed if call
1997:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            'OSTaskCreate()'.
1998:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
1999:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              id            is the task's ID (0..65535)
2000:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
2001:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              stk_size      is the size of the stack (in 'stack units').  If the stack units are I
2002:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            then, 'stk_size' contains the number of bytes for the stack.  If the s
2003:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            units are INT32Us then, the stack contains '4 * stk_size' bytes.  The 
2004:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            units are established by the #define constant OS_STK which is CPU
2005:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            specific.  'stk_size' is 0 if called by 'OSTaskCreate()'.
2006:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
2007:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              pext          is a pointer to a user supplied memory area that is used to extend the
2008:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            control block.  This allows you to store the contents of floating-poin
2009:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            registers, MMU registers or anything else you could find useful during
2010:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            context switch.  You can even assign a name to each task and store thi
2011:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            in this TCB extension.  A NULL pointer is passed if called by OSTaskCr
2012:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
2013:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              opt           options as passed to 'OSTaskCreateExt()' or,
2014:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                            0 if called from 'OSTaskCreate()'.
2015:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
2016:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** * Returns    : OS_ERR_NONE              if the call was successful
2017:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *              OS_ERR_TASK_NO_MORE_TCB  if there are no more free TCBs to be allocated and thus, th
2018:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *                                       cannot be created.
2019:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** *
2020:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** * Note       : This function is INTERNAL to uC/OS-II and your application should not call it.
2021:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
2022:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** */
2023:./ucos/Core/os_core.c **** 
